  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_76512f19e35c456f9178f0137297e127",
      "statement": "step ca renew validates flags: --expires-in and --renew-period are incompatible, --renew-period requires --daemon, --pid and --pid-file are mutually exclusive (pid-file is parsed to a positive integer), --renew-period and --expires-in must each be shorter than the certificate validity period, and the key pair is loaded KMS-aware via tlsLoadX509KeyPair.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L233-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00969ead325b6bea32e89cd4f00bd70a139ec7c799b790785d7dc29cf38ff32a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27b4788471374b009919606b9df0fe9e",
      "statement": "In one-shot mode with --expires-in, the certificate is renewed only when its remaining lifetime is within expiresIn plus a non-cryptographic jitter of rand.Int63n(expiresIn/20), otherwise it prints 'certificate not renewed' and exits successfully.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L336-L351",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fbdbdcf524979596aeb09909ef4a4527eb9f66237f6f5b7b7acd349981a6ff9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_efb0427c9d00498393440e0bfe5b0180",
      "statement": "Daemon scheduling in nextRenewDuration uses --renew-period when set (renew now if expiry is within the period, else wait the period), otherwise waits until time.Until(NotAfter) minus --expires-in with random jitter up to period/20; with neither flag expiresIn defaults to one third of the validity period, so the daemon renews before 2/3 of the validity has elapsed, as the help text states.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L213-L225",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0163a0dbc1ecf0b0267ab7b32258180ad5be1fd7608debf178c3a6520ede31fd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L354-L380",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01ffbad2ae3f1aae3edb8f558cef5e6ddc34ca88f58078614ce4581c2896bcf8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38e02f30b5e345edac487c3644c0dd47",
      "statement": "The renew daemon selects on SIGINT/SIGTERM (exit) and SIGHUP (immediate renewal) plus a timer; after each renewal it runs --pid/--pid-file signaling with --signal (default SIGHUP) and an --exec command split on whitespace with inherited stdio, and RenewAndPrepareNext reloads the new chain into the transport and reschedules errors after 1 minute.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L382-L413",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96e14aa62f14f466cf7166796955a3e1d3e828741e001dafa97445b0f428cdb7:"
